This couldn't be further from the truth

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.920
After researching how lions actually behave in the wild,

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:07.100
I've come to learn what would've really happened here, is a far darker,

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.140
and far bloodier story.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:13.000
There is no hakuna matata in today's theory my friends, let's begin.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.840
To start off with, in order to understand the society of the lions we are talking about,

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:21.760
we first have to understand what kind of lions Mufasa, Scar and Simba actually are.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:29.600
I mean this live action remake portrays them as real lions, so they have to be based off of real animals somewhere  along the line here, right?

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:34.720
Well, surprisingly it's actually easy to find out the exact sub-species of lion we are talking about.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:38.520
When researching for the film, the producers, director and other lead crew

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:42.060
took a trip to 'Hell's Gate National Park' in Kenya, Africa.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.620
This would end up being what the entire film was based off of.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:49.540
Pride rock, it's an actual real place in 'Hell's Gate'

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.540
Being set in Kenya would make the lions we see in The Lion King

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:56.280
the Panthera Leo Melanochaita, or East African Lion.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:00.620
But we can get even more specific here, let's look a bit closer at the character models for Scar and Simba,

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:04.160
notice these extra tufts of hair on their knee joints?

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.220
This isn't just a little extra animation,

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:09.300
this clearly identifies them as Masai Lions.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:13.580
So, with that knowledge in hand, we can actually analyse what their society looks like

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:19.660
and how, in nearly every way, Scar is genetically superior to Mufasa.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:24.080
You see, us humans view Mufasa with utmost respect and Scar as the villain,

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:26.980
because, well, he has a scar. And that makes him evil.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:30.820
However it turns out that choosy lionesses choose scar,

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:32.880
Look again at Mufasa, Scar and Simba.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:40.000
we see the tufts of fur on both Scar and Simba's knees but you'll notice that Mufasa is distinctly missing those exact same tufts.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:45.540
Now, while it may be extreme to call it a genetic defect, the fact that he can't grow that extra hair on his knees,

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:51.180
is our first hint that Mufasa is actually a genetically inferior male lion.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.260
Just like the fact that I'm incapable of growing a beard makes me-

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:54.940
You know what? Never mind, bad comparison.

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:59.860
But it's less of what Mufasa doesn't have and more of what Scar does that matters:

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.880
A beautiful, dark mane.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:06.100
That again,  is not just an artistic choice to make Scar dark and brooding,

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:09.460
according to research done at the University of Minnesota, don't ya' know?

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:16.060
Lions with dark manes are actually much more attractive to female lions than those with lighter manes.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:21.800
In The Lion Kingdom, dark manes are actually a sign of lions with higher testosterone levels.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:24.200
In a nature.com article covering the study,

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.900
Quote: "Males with high levels of testosterone grow darker hair

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:33.000
These males may be more aggressive and therefore better at defending mates and cubs." End quote.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:38.700
This, in turn, gives their offspring a higher chance of survival, which in the animal kingdom, is a BIG deal.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:43.240
I guess in any kingdom that's kind of a big deal,  no one really wants their children to die

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:47.360
early, horrific deaths. But you know, animals care a lot about this stuff.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:52.860
Furthermore, lions with more testosterone  also tend to have longer reproductive lifespans,

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.400
which means that Scar is gonna be rockin' Pride Rock much longer than his brother.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:00.280
That's right, Scar is a literal sexy beast with those dark locks of his.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:06.940
Now, let me clear something up right here, lion society does not function like a human monarchy like we see in the movie.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:11.900
We are led to believe that since Simba is born of the current king, he is next in line to take the throne.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.200
That is just simply wrong!

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.680
Simba was most likely gonna get himself booted out of the Pride no matter what,

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:22.820
dead dad or otherwise. When young male cubs approach full adult male status,

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:25.640
they are actually exiled from the Pride.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:30.200
Renowned National Geographic filmmaker Dereck Joubert said in an article in Live Science

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:37.100
Quote: "When male lions begin to reach sexual maturity around age 2, the older males within the pride kick them out." End quote.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.820
Why would this be? you ask. One word:

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:45.700
Incest. Think about it, you're the king and as a result you're the one making most if not all of the babies.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.060
