00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:10.240
You just understood the concept, can you feel the love tonight?

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.540
I certainly can, but I don't wanna

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:17.140
To avoid these sorts of awkward run-ins, the young male lions are kicked out of the pride.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.940
Where they go on to form small groups called coalitions.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:27.040
Quote from Luke Hunter, President of Panthera. Which, based on the name, is either a big cat conservation or

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.120
a feline themed super-villain society. I'll leave it up to you to judge.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:37.200
Quote: "After being kicked out, the young males roam the countryside solo or in small bands, often with their brothers or cousins,

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.220
negotiating the no-cat's-land between territories of other lions.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.900
They usually do this as a coalition." End quote.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:48.660
These coalitions begins roaming around in search of territory or a pride they can take over

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:55.520
When a coalition finds an optimal pride, they may challenge the current reigning lions with a fight TO THE DEATH.

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:58.500
Usually, sometimes they retreat but mostly it's TO THE DEATH.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:02.300
If the coalition is successful, they then take over the pride and reign over it.

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:06.100
So, how this would have really gone down prior to the events that we see in the movie

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:12.140
is that a young Mufasa and a young Scar would've been part of one of these exiled coalitions,

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:16.400
they would've come along the reigning lions at Pride Rock, defeated them and taken over.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:20.220
Scar probably loses a battle of dominance against Mufasa the first time,

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:25.280
which is why we see Mufasa as the reigning king, but comes back to challenge him a second time at the Gorge.

